.TH ZDOTS-ENDPOINTS 1 "2026-07-21" "zdots" "zdots manual"
.SH NAME
zdots-endpoints \- bin/zdots\-endpoints — verify the nginx\-proxied web endpoints (.localhost / .local)
.SH SYNOPSIS
See OPTIONS below (generated from \fBzdots-endpoints --help\fR).
.SH OPTIONS
.nf
bin/zdots-endpoints — verify the nginx-proxied web endpoints (.localhost / .local)

Discovers every endpoint from two sources — *.localhost names from the
deployed nginx server_names (RFC 6761: always loopback, never in /etc/hosts)
and *.local names from /etc/hosts (the mDNS namespace: needs an explicit
pinned entry, see decision-011) — probes each through the full chain
(resolution → nginx → TLS → upstream), and prints a status table with
clickable links to open each interface and the command to tail its log.
Cross-checks against the deployed nginx vhosts to flag hosts that resolve but
have no server block, and flags any *.local host not pointed at loopback.

Usage:
  zdots-endpoints            Status table (default)
  zdots-endpoints logs HOST  Tail the log for HOST (e.g. llama.localhost)
  zdots-endpoints open HOST  Open HOST's interface in the browser
  zdots-endpoints -q         Quiet: only non-healthy rows
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
agent-guide(1), zdots-doctor(1)
